    "body": "## Hephaisto's plan for this issue\n\n**Summary.** FAKE SDK plan: Endpoints.Primary checks options.Endpoints.Count without a null check, so an absent Shop:Endpoints section crashes startup with a NullReferenceException.\n\n**What is wrong, and what will change.** src/Shop.Api/Startup/Endpoints.cs:17 dereferences options.Endpoints, which the binder leaves null (not empty) when Shop:Endpoints is absent; the code guards only against an empty list.\n\n**Files**\n- `src/Shop.Api/Startup/Endpoints.cs`\n\n**Steps**\n1. Treat a null Endpoints list as empty in Endpoints.Primary.\n2. Keep EndpointsOptionsTests.Empty_endpoints_do_not_throw green; do not add configuration under deploy/.\n\n**Verification.** The change will be covered by tests that the Job runs before it opens the pull request.\n\n**Cost of planning.** $0.00 · the plan's own confidence is 0.90\n\n---\n\n**To go ahead,** an approver replies `/approve`. **To refuse it,** an approver replies `/reject <reason>`. The command is the first line of the comment, and only an approver of this install is heard.\n\nWhat is approved is this plan as Hephaisto stored it - not the text of this comment, and not the issue as it may read by then. An approval starts a Job that works on branch `hephaisto/codefix-28742a5a8a24` and opens a draft pull request; a person reviews and merges it.\n\n<sub>Attempt `01a11846-a0c1-7a5f-9131-28742a5a8a24` · analysed at `583b1e5b75ad`</sub>\n<!-- hephaisto:plan:01a11846a0c17a5f913128742a5a8a24 -->",
